  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The bridal shawl is worked from the top neck edge downward. Each RS row adds one extra "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-fan"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble fan"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " repeat at each side of centre. The result is a triangle that widens evenly. A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "deep-picot-border"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "deep picot border"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " runs around all three sides after the body is complete."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work at a tighter-than-usual tension for lace weight: the fabric should hold its shape without stiffness. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "lace-blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking with wires"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is strongly advised. Allow around 800 m."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Lace-weight yarn",
              "qty": "800 m"
            },
            {
              "name": "3.5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation and setup"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 7. Row 1: 1 dc in 4th ch from hook, ch 2, 7 tr into last ch (first "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-fan"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "fan"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "), ch 2, 1 dc in same ch. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every RS row: work ch 5, dc, ch 2, fan, ch 2, dc at centre point, then mirror on opposite side. Increase by one fan group per side per RS row. Continue until wingspan reaches 170 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Edging"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Attach yarn at one corner. Row 1: dc across all edges. Row 2: ch 4, skip 2 dc, repeat. Row 3 (picot): dc in arch, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "deep-picot-border"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ch 3, sl st in 1st ch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", dc in same arch, repeat. This completes the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "deep-picot-border"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "deep picot border"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Blocking"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thread "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "lace-blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blocking wires"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " through the points along all three sides before pinning. Mist with water and leave to dry on a foam mat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
